## Instructions
Decide if this person is worth reaching out to. Apply a GENEROUS standard — your default should be YES.

Only disqualify if there is a clear, obvious reason this person could never be a relevant prospect (e.g. student with no business role, retired, completely unrelated industry with no plausible connection to our product).

A soft or partial match is enough to qualify. Someone adjacent to the ICP, in a related industry, or at a company that could plausibly benefit counts as qualified. We would rather send an extra message to a borderline lead than miss someone good.

Do NOT disqualify based on:
- Seniority being too low or too high
- Company size being uncertain
- Title not being an exact match to the ICP
- Lack of explicit decision-making authority

